    "sensesNotes": "Darkvision 30 ft, Blood Scent",
    "tactics": "Piranha Swarms attack the most wounded swimmer first and stay on that target until it escapes the water or stops bleeding. They avoid armored creatures if an unarmored target is available, but their numbers make them dangerous around capsized boats and wrecks.",
    "attacksNotes": "<p>Frenzied Bites: Opposed Reflex save using Agil 7 + Melee Combat 3 against every creature sharing the swarm's space. Target loses: 8 piercing damage. Target wins: 4 piercing damage. At half HP or lower, deal 4 piercing damage on a loss and 2 piercing damage on a win.</p>",
    "specialAbilitiesNotes": "<p>Blood Frenzy: Against a creature below half HP, the Piranha Swarm subtracts 1 from both attack dice. Schooling: The Piranha Swarm can move through the spaces of other creatures without provoking opportunity ### Attacks. Blood Scent: The Piranha Swarm has Fortune on Perception checks to locate a creature that has taken damage in the water. Swarms: Swarms occupy a 5 × 5 ft space, halve physical damage, ignore Grappled, Restrained, Prone, and Bleeding, and resolve their ### Attacks as opposed Reflex saves. Each entry lists full damage and reduced damage once the swarm is at half HP or lower.</p>",
